{"id": "methodology-001", "family": "methodology", "question": "What is ZORI?", "expected_tool": "search_knowledge", "expected_response": "answer", "first_output_valid": true, "first_tool": "search_knowledge", "tool_correct": true, "kind": "answer", "kind_correct": true, "plan_match": null, "exec_match": null, "answer_source": "model", "faithful": true, "success": true, "latency_ms": 1141.7, "model_calls": 2, "answer": "ZORI is a measure of typical market rents, calculated as a repeat-rent index that compares the asking rents of the same rental units over time. It covers April 2015 to the latest month and is not a sale price or signed lease, but rather a representation of what rents are being asked for similar properties.", "failures": [], "planner_outputs": ["{\"call\": {\"tool\": \"search_knowledge\", \"query\": \"ZORI definition\"}}"], "plan": null, "trace": [{"step": 1, "tool": "search_knowledge", "status": "ok", "duration_ms": 0.1, "detail": "3 passages"}, {"step": 2, "tool": "answer_writer", "status": "ok", "duration_ms": 0.0, "detail": "answer"}]}
{"id": "methodology-002", "family": "methodology", "question": "How is ZHVI calculated?", "expected_tool": "search_knowledge", "expected_response": "answer", "first_output_valid": true, "first_tool": "search_knowledge", "tool_correct": true, "kind": "answer", "kind_correct": true, "plan_match": null, "exec_match": null, "answer_source": "model", "faithful": true, "success": true, "latency_ms": 990.9, "model_calls": 2, "answer": "ZHVI is calculated as a trimmed mean of the middle third of Zestimates, Zillow's estimated values for individual homes, updated monthly with a repeat-Zestimate method. The model was updated in 2023 with a neural-network model, which improved tracking of market turning points.", "failures": [], "planner_outputs": ["{\"call\": {\"tool\": \"search_knowledge\", \"query\": \"ZHVI methodology\"}}"], "plan": null, "trace": [{"step": 1, "tool": "search_knowledge", "status": "ok", "duration_ms": 0.2, "detail": "3 passages"}, {"step": 2, "tool": "answer_writer", "status": "ok", "duration_ms": 0.0, "detail": "answer"}]}
{"id": "methodology-003", "family": "methodology", "question": "What does smoothed and seasonally adjusted mean for these indices?", "expected_tool": "search_knowledge", "expected_response": "answer", "first_output_valid": true, "first_tool": "search_knowledge", "tool_correct": true, "kind": "answer", "kind_correct": true, "plan_match": null, "exec_match": null, "answer_source": "model", "faithful": true, "success": true, "latency_ms": 911.7, "model_calls": 2, "answer": "Smoothing reduces month-to-month volatility, and seasonally adjusting removes the yearly cycle, so changes in these indices reflect the underlying trend. ZORI is smoothed with a three-month moving average and seasonally adjusted, which helps identify the long-term direction.", "failures": [], "planner_outputs": ["{\"call\": {\"tool\": \"search_knowledge\", \"query\": \"smoothing seasonal adjustment\"}}"], "plan": null, "trace": [{"step": 1, "tool": "search_knowledge", "status": "ok", "duration_ms": 0.1, "detail": "3 passages"}, {"step": 2, "tool": "answer_writer", "status": "ok", "duration_ms": 0.0, "detail": "answer"}]}
